{#-
Gluon FlexAttention forward for CDNA4 (gfx950).

Semantics follow flex_attention.py.jinja: score_mod sees qk * SM_SCALE, the
softmax runs in base 2, LSE and MAX are stored in log2 units, and the
block-sparse loop visits partial blocks (score_mod + mask_mod) and then full
blocks (score_mod only).

The kernel is persistent: NUM_PROGRAMS programs loop over (batch, head, query
block) work items in a swizzled order (see the scheduler comment below).

The MFMA/dot-operand layouts, padded shared layouts and async K/V staging are
adapted from the gfx950 Gluon MHA prefill kernel in tokenspeed
(https://github.com/lightseekorg/tokenspeed, tokenspeed-kernel-amd), used under
the MIT License:

